  {
   "id": "crush-functions-md-13",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Concurrency: `spawn`, `yield`, `async`, `await`\n\nThese keywords are in the grammar, but the end-to-end path is incomplete: a\nprogram that contains `spawn f()`, `async fn`, or `await` is rejected by the\nassembler (`SPAWN takes 1 operand(s), got 0`). The AI/concurrency opcodes are\ntracked under crush-ast **CRUSH-1** / **CRUSH-34**. A bare `yield` statement\ncompiles and runs (it is a no-op without a spawned task).\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-8",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn worker() {\n    print(\"worker\")\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    spawn worker()\n    yield\n    print(\"main\")\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
