  {
   "id": "crush-functions-md-15",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Best practices\n\n- Keep functions small and give parameters type hints — they document the\n  interface and catch mistakes at compile time.\n- Pass data in as parameters: functions cannot see top-level variables\n  ([Variables](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/variables.html#module-level-variables-are-not-visible-inside-functions)).\n- Prefer descriptive names (`calculate_total_price`, not `calc`).\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- **[Capability System](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/capabilities.html)**\n- **[Polyglot Programming](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/polyglot.html)**\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  }
 ]
